course: dictionary
lesson: 8347
title: A roost, and rule the roost
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a thing, an action, or part of a saying, and «roost» can be all three. Read the words around it to find out which one you have. «The owl came back to its roost in the old barn» uses roost as a place. In «The birds roost in the trees at night», it is an action.
explain: Look for clues. In «The bats roost in the roof all summer», the clues are all, summer and roof. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The bats settle down to rest in the roof all summer" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Some words belong to sayings, and the saying does not mean what the words say alone. «She likes to rule the roost» does not mean she sits on a roof. It means she is the boss. When you meet a saying, read the whole sentence first and ask what the people are doing and who is in charge.
fact: A roost is a place where birds or bats rest or sleep, such as a branch, a perch or a barn.
fact: To roost means for birds or bats to settle down to rest or sleep there.
fact: «Rule the roost» means to be the boss of a group or a home.
fact: «Come home to roost» means that bad things someone did come back to cause trouble for them.
fact: Bat roosts are protected by law in the UK, because bats lose their roosts easily.
exercise: «In winter the crows gather in a roost of hundreds at night.» What is a roost here? | *A place where birds rest or sleep | A cold winter day | A kind of bird with a loud call | A tall cathedral tower
exercise: «She likes to rule the roost at home.» What does rule the roost mean? | To fly high over the trees | To feel very tired | *To be the boss | To sleep on the roof
exercise: «The noctule flies high, then roosts in old woodpecker holes.» Find and copy the word that means settle down to rest or sleep. | high | holes | *roosts | flies
test: «He had been unkind for years, and now his bad deeds came home to roost.» What does came home to roost mean? | *Bad things came back to cause him trouble | He went home early after school | He found a lost bird and took it home | He had a long rest in the sun
test: «British bats raise one baby a year in summer roosts in roofs and trees.» What is a summer roost? | A warm wind that blows in July | A bat's favourite food | A summer holiday for birds | *A place where bats rest or sleep in summer
exam: Why are bat roosts protected by law? | *Because bats lose their roosts easily | Because bats are very large and heavy | Because roosts are made of gold | Because bats sing all night long
